## 3. Run Shapiro-Wilk on body mass

Run `shapiro.test()` on the non-missing Chinstrap body-mass values. Save the result as `shapiro_mass` and print it.

::: {.callout-note appearance="simple"}
## Reading Shapiro-Wilk output

The null hypothesis is **normality**. A **small p-value** (conventionally below 0.05) means the data look **inconsistent with** a normal distribution. A **large p-value** means you do **not** have evidence against normality — not proof that the data are perfectly normal.
:::




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='warmup_shapiro'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: warmup_shapiro
shapiro_mass <- 

```
:::




::: {.hint exercise="warmup_shapiro"}
::: {.callout-note collapse="false"}
## Hint

From `?shapiro.test`: pass a numeric vector directly. Drop missing values first:

```r
shapiro.test(mtcars$mpg)
```

Use the body-mass column from `chinstrap`, skipping NAs.
:::
:::

::: {.solution exercise="warmup_shapiro"}
::: {.callout-tip collapse="false"}
## Solution

```r
shapiro_mass <- shapiro.test(chinstrap$body_mass_g)
shapiro_mass
```

You should see p ≈ 0.56 — no evidence against normality for body mass.
:::
:::




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='warmup_shapiro' check='true'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: warmup_shapiro
#| check: true
code <- paste(.user_code, collapse = "\n")
if (!grepl("shapiro\\.test\\s*\\(", code)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "error",
    message = "Call `shapiro.test()` on Chinstrap body mass."
  )
} else if (!exists("shapiro_mass", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "warning",
    message = "Save the result as `shapiro_mass`."
  )
} else {
  sm <- get("shapiro_mass", envir = .envir_result)
  if (!is.null(sm$p.value) && sm$p.value > 0.05) {
    list(
      correct = TRUE,
      type = "success",
      message = paste0("p = ", signif(sm$p.value, 3), " — no evidence against normality. Good warm-up.")
    )
  } else {
    list(
      correct = TRUE,
      type = "success",
      message = "Shapiro-Wilk ran. Compare your p-value to 0.05."
    )
  }
}
```
:::




