:::




::: {.hint exercise="mean_raw"}
::: {.callout-note collapse="false"}
## Hint

From `?mean`: `mean(x, na.rm = FALSE)` — set `na.rm = TRUE` to skip missing values.

```r
mean(mtcars$mpg, na.rm = TRUE)
```

Apply to `tick_data$tick_count`.
:::
:::

::: {.solution exercise="mean_raw"}
::: {.callout-tip collapse="false"}
## Solution

```r
mean_raw <- mean(tick_data$tick_count, na.rm = TRUE)
mean_raw
```

You should see about 12.9 — close to the reference value of 13.
:::
:::




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='mean_raw' check='true'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: mean_raw
#| check: true
code <- paste(.user_code, collapse = "\n")
if (!grepl("mean\\s*\\(", code)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "error",
    message = "Use `mean()` on `tick_data$tick_count`."
  )
} else if (!grepl("na\\.rm\\s*=\\s*TRUE", code, ignore.case = TRUE)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "info",
    message = "Include `na.rm = TRUE` inside `mean()`."
  )
} else if (!exists("mean_raw", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "warning",
    message = "Save the result as `mean_raw`."
  )
} else {
  mr <- get("mean_raw", envir = .envir_result)
  if (is.numeric(mr) && length(mr) == 1 && !is.na(mr) && mr > 12 && mr < 14) {
    list(
      correct = TRUE,
      type = "success",
      message = paste0("Mean ≈ ", round(mr, 2), " ticks — close to the reference of 13.")
    )
  } else {
    list(
      correct = FALSE,
      type = "info",
      message = "Compute `mean_raw <- mean(tick_data$tick_count, na.rm = TRUE)`."
    )
  }
}
```
:::




## 6. Trim impossible values

**Step 1 — trim impossible values.** Remove rows where `tick_count` is negative (a sign error). **Keep** rows where `tick_count` is missing. Save the result as `tick_clean`.

::: {.callout-note appearance="simple"}
## `|` means "or"

Inside `filter()`, the vertical bar **`|`** means **"or"**. The condition `is.na(tick_count) | tick_count >= 0` keeps a row if **either** the count is missing **or** it is zero or positive.

Writing `filter(tick_count >= 0)` alone silently **drops the missing rows** — because `NA >= 0` evaluates to `NA`, not `TRUE`.
:::




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='trim_impossible'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: trim_impossible
tick_clean <- tick_data |>

```
:::




::: {.hint exercise="trim_impossible"}
::: {.callout-note collapse="false"}
## Hint

From `?filter`: keep rows where conditions are TRUE.

```r
mtcars |>
  filter(is.na(mpg) | mpg >= 0)
```

Keep missing tick counts **or** non-negative counts.
:::
:::

::: {.solution exercise="trim_impossible"}
::: {.callout-tip collapse="false"}
## Solution

```r
tick_clean <- tick_data |>
  filter(is.na(tick_count) | tick_count >= 0)
```

66 rows — two negative sign errors removed, three missing values kept.
:::
:::




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='trim_impossible' check='true'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: trim_impossible
#| check: true
code <- paste(.user_code, collapse = "\n")
if (!exists("tick_clean", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "warning",
    message = "Save the filtered table as `tick_clean`."
  )
} else {
  tc <- get("tick_clean", envir = .envir_result)
  n <- nrow(tc)
  n_na <- sum(is.na(tc$tick_count))
  n_neg <- sum(!is.na(tc$tick_count) & tc$tick_count < 0)
  used_or <- grepl("is\\.na\\s*\\(\\s*tick_count\\s*\\)", code) && grepl("\\|", code)
  if (n == 66 && n_na == 3 && n_neg == 0) {
    list(
      correct = TRUE,
      type = "success",
      message = "66 rows — negatives gone, missing values kept."
    )
  } else if (n == 63 && n_na == 0) {
    list(
      correct = FALSE,
      type = "error",
      message = "`filter(tick_count >= 0)` alone drops missing rows. Use `is.na(tick_count) | tick_count >= 0`."
    )
  } else if (!used_or) {
    list(
      correct = FALSE,
      type = "info",
      message = "Use `filter(is.na(tick_count) | tick_count >= 0)` so missing rows stay."
    )
  } else {
    list(
      correct = FALSE,
      type = "info",
      message = "Filter with `is.na(tick_count) | tick_count >= 0` and save as `tick_clean`."
    )
  }
}
```
:::




## 7. Flag distributional outliers

**Step 2 — flag outliers.** Using only the non-missing tick counts in `tick_clean`, calculate the upper fence of the 1.5 × IQR rule: Q3 + 1.5 × IQR. Save it as `upper_fence` and print it. Do not remove any rows.




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' setup='true' exercise='upper_fence'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| setup: true
#| exercise: upper_fence
library(tidyverse)
library(palmerpenguins)
chinstrap <- penguins |> filter(species == "Chinstrap")
tick_counts <- c(
  11, 17, 21, 9, 10, 4, 12, NA, 30, 20, 15, 10, -1, 10, 11, 19, 13, 21,
  7, 12, 20, 18, 8, 26, 6, 10, 6, 7, 14, 7, NA, 3, 12, 13, 5, 10, 19, 24,
  10, 14, 14, -3, 8, 17, 16, 7, 14, 2, 9, 10, 10, 13, 12, 16, NA, 15, 33,
  11, 13, 14, 5, 15, 27, 15, 18, 10, 30, 6
)
tick_data <- chinstrap |>
  mutate(penguin_id = paste0("CS", sprintf("%03d", row_number())), tick_count = tick_counts)
tick_clean <- tick_data |>
  filter(is.na(tick_count) | tick_count >= 0)
```
:::

::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='upper_fence'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: upper_fence
upper_fence <- 

```
:::




::: {.hint exercise="upper_fence"}
::: {.callout-note collapse="false"}
## Hint

From `?quantile`: `quantile(x, probs, na.rm = FALSE)`. From `?IQR`: `IQR(x, na.rm = FALSE)`.

```r
q3 <- quantile(mtcars$mpg, 0.75, na.rm = TRUE)
fence <- q3 + 1.5 * IQR(mtcars$mpg, na.rm = TRUE)
```

Use the 75th percentile and IQR of non-missing tick counts.
:::
:::

::: {.solution exercise="upper_fence"}
::: {.callout-tip collapse="false"}
## Solution

```r
upper_fence <- quantile(tick_clean$tick_count, 0.75, na.rm = TRUE) +
  1.5 * IQR(tick_clean$tick_count, na.rm = TRUE)
upper_fence
```

The upper fence is 27 — three penguins have tick counts above it.
:::
:::




::: {.cell envir='assumptions_lab' exercise='upper_fence' check='true'}
```{webr}
#| envir: assumptions_lab
#| exercise: upper_fence
#| check: true
code <- paste(.user_code, collapse = "\n")
if (!exists("upper_fence", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
  list(
    correct = FALSE,
    type = "warning",
    message = "Save the result as `upper_fence`."
  )
} else {
  uf <- as.numeric(get("upper_fence", envir = .envir_result))
  has_q <- grepl("quantile\\s*\\(", code)
  has_iqr <- grepl("IQR\\s*\\(", code)
  if (length(uf) == 1 && abs(uf - 27) < 0.5 && has_q && has_iqr) {
    list(
      correct = TRUE,
      type = "success",
      message = "Upper fence = 27. Three counts sit above it — flag them, do not delete them yet."
    )
  } else if (has_q && has_iqr) {
    list(
      correct = TRUE,
      type = "success",
      message = paste0("Upper fence ≈ ", round(uf, 1), ". Check how many counts exceed it.")
    )
  } else {
    list(
      correct = FALSE,
      type = "info",
      message = "Use `quantile(..., 0.75, na.rm = TRUE) + 1.5 * IQR(..., na.rm = TRUE)`."
    )
  }
}
```
:::




